-- title:
--   Kernel of ρ is a minimal prime over (varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ over $L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. generated over $L$ by the image under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L : \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma0 (M * p))`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, together with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K_2$; let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $j_2 \in K_2$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,L$ applied to the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNum}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the modular invariant. Write $C = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_2\,j_2$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$, and $\mathrm{jChartFin}$ for $j_2$ regarded in $C$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : C \to \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M$ be a ring homomorphism into the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ generated over $k$ by $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k = q^{-1}\,\mathrm{jNum}_k$ and its $M$-fold $q$-expansion substitute $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,M$, such that: $\rho$ kills the image of $\varpi$; $\rho(\mathrm{jChartFin}) = \mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,M$, the element $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k$ of that field; and every $f$ in the target admits $a, b$ in the $k$-subalgebra generated by the range of $\rho$ with $b \ne 0$ and $f b = a$. Then $\ker \rho$ is a minimal prime over the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the minimality step in the description of the special fibre at $p$ of the integral model of $X_0(Mp)$ built from two $j$-charts: a birational, $\varpi$-killing specialisation of the chart algebra onto the level-$M$ function field in characteristic $p$ cuts out a whole irreducible component of the fibre, not a smaller closed subset such as a supersingular point. It is used in the identification of $\ker \rho$ with the non-units of a Gauss valuation subring, and thence in the Deligne–Rapoport style analysis of the two components of the mod $p$ fibre.
